{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-02T09:16:36.592Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"7687d94a08e852f40579b9f7","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-csv-lewj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Resource admission drops installed extension type/field registries from validation and revision lookup"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Tracks gh:unbraind/pm-csv#214 (filed 2026-10-29, missed by the blind issue watch). admission.ts on current main still calls resolveItemTypeRegistry(settings) without the active workspace extension registrations in both scan() and the revision-lookup path (locateItem type_to_folder), so an installed extension-defined item type becomes a row_invalid admission rejection and revision reads use a narrower schema than the writer. Verified on main 2026-11-02: the one-argument resolver call remains. The bounded-admission feature that delivered PR #213 is closed, so this regression needs its own fix: activate the target workspace extensions (or pass the resolved registry) before scan and revision lookup, and add an admission regression with an extension-defined type and field."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["admission","extensions","gh:unbraind/pm-csv#214"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-02T09:16:36.592Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-02T09:16:36.592Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-glm"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","